{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A heifer three-year-old, and a she-goat three-year-old.</b> Rabbi Abraham [Ibn Ezra] explained: in its third year. But Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 15:9) rendered 'three,' and so is the correct interpretation, for a three-year-old is not called עֶגְלָה, as we learned in the Mishnah (Parah 1:1): 'And the Sages say: עֶגְלָה is a two-year-old, פָּרָה is a three-year-old.' And he hinted that from them his offspring will offer three categories of offering before Him — the burnt offering, the sin offering, and the peace offering — for the guilt offering is like the sin offering; there is no difference between them except the designation alone. And it is possible that the reason for 'מְשֻׁלֶּשֶׁת' (trebled) is that he would bring them in sets of three, each kind separately, and so too 'כִּי מְשֻׁלָּשׁוֹת הֵנָּה' (Ezekiel 42:6), for there were upper chambers, middle ones, and lower ones."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "In Parah 1:1 the reading is עֶגְלָה בַּת שְׁתַּיִם וּפָרָה בַּת שָׁלֹשׁ; I have translated Ramban's citation faithfully as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:30:07.355429948Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}